Algorithmic influences and attributions (clean-room — read for understanding)
================================================================================
  B. Lévy, S. Petitjean, N. Ray, J. Maillot. "Least Squares Conformal Maps for
  Automatic Texture Atlas Generation." SIGGRAPH 2002. (The founding auto-atlas
  pipeline: segmentation + conformal flattening + packing.)

  P. Sander, J. Snyder, S. Gortler, H. Hoppe. "Texture Mapping Progressive
  Meshes." SIGGRAPH 2001. (The texture stretch metric.)

  A. Sheffer, B. Lévy, et al. "ABF++: Fast and Robust Angle Based Flattening."
  ACM TOG 2005.

  L. Liu, L. Zhang, Y. Xu, C. Gotsman, S. Gortler. "A Local/Global Approach to
  Mesh Parameterization." (ARAP parameterization, SGP 2008.)

  M. Rabinovich, R. Poranne, O. Sorkine-Hornung. "Scalable Locally Injective
  Mappings." (SLIM, ACM TOG 2017.)

  R. Sawhney, K. Crane. "Boundary First Flattening." (ACM TOG 2018.)

See docs/design/references.md for the full bibliography.

================================================================================
Reference oracle (test-only; not shipped, not linked)
================================================================================
Golden UV layouts/metrics are generated by a trusted external unwrapper (e.g.
xatlas, MIT; or Blender, GPL, run headless) invoked as an external process; no
code from them is included or redistributed.

================================================================================
Third-party runtime dependencies
================================================================================
The core ships dependency-light. Permissively-licensed managed packages are added
per phase (docs/plans/02-phase-roadmap.md) and listed here as they land:

  CSparse.NET   sparse direct/iterative linear solves (LSCM/ARAP)   (MIT)

Native UV/parameterization libraries (xatlas, Microsoft UVAtlas, libigl, CGAL)
are NOT taken as runtime dependencies; CGAL's surface-mesh parameterization is
GPL and is deliberately avoided.
